---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Commit Extension — who runs the shop you're on, and where your friends shop"
  description="Reads the org.nr a Norwegian shop prints and shows years in operation, employees and revenue from Brønnøysundregistrene. Friends can share a shop card made from their own browsing. Nothing to type. Open source."
  canonical="https://getcommit.dev/extension/"
>

  <!-- Nav -->
  <nav>
    <div class="container nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="nav-brand">Commit</a>
      <ul class="nav-links">
        <li><a href="/audit">Audit</a></li>
        <li><a href="/extension" style="color: var(--ink);">Extension</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog">Writing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li><li><a href="/docs">Docs</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <span class="hero-eyebrow">Browser extension · Free · Open source · v0.5.0</span>
        <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);">
          Who runs this shop,<br /><em>and who you know shops there.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          Norwegian shops print their organisation number in the footer. The extension reads it and puts one line
          in the corner: how long the company has existed, how many people work there, what it sold last year.
          Nobody types anything, and you don't need an account or friends to get it.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/releases/download/v0.5.0/commit-extension-v0.5.0.zip" class="btn-primary">Download v0.5.0 →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/releases" class="btn-ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">All releases →</a>
        </div>
        <p id="kort"><small>Got a card link from someone? Install the extension, then open the link again and click «Importer».</small></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <h2>What it shows</h2>
        <p><strong>On the shop.</strong> «Biltema Norge AS · i drift siden 2000 · 1 845 ansatte · omsetning 2025: 5,6 mrd kr».
        The figures come from Brønnøysundregistrene. The line turns red only on hard facts: bankruptcy or liquidation,
        a company registered less than a year ago with no accounts, or an org.nr belonging to a company whose name
        doesn't resemble the domain (a rough check, and the line says so). If the page has no org.nr, you get nothing.
        The extension never guesses an org.nr from a name.</p>
        <p><strong>Under search results.</strong> The same line on Google and Bing, for shops whose org.nr you've already seen on an earlier visit.</p>
        <p><strong>Mitt kort.</strong> Your browser keeps its own list of shops you come back to over several months and the
        order confirmations you reach. You can see the list in the extension menu, remove any row, and send it as a link.
        A friend who imports it sees «Håkon: handlet her 3× (2025–26)» on that shop and under its results.
        Health, pharmacy, gambling, dating, adult sites, religion, politics, banks and loans are never counted.</p>
        <p><strong>GitHub.</strong> A trust card on repository pages: age, recent activity, contributors, releases.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="personvern">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>The org.nr that a shop page prints goes to data.brreg.no, the public registry, and nothing is sent with it.
        Your shop list stays in your browser. It leaves only when you copy the link and send it yourself. The card data sits
        after the <code>#</code> in that link, so even getcommit.dev's server doesn't see it when your friend opens it.
        No Commit server stores anyone's browsing or purchases.</p>
        <p>Two lookups do go to Commit's servers, without any account attached. On a GitHub repository page the
        extension sends the owner and repository name to fetch the trust card, and opening the toolbar popup
        looks up the current tab's domain.
        Visit-time sharing is off by default; if you turn it on in the popup, visited domains and time spent are sent every five minutes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="install">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <p>The extension is not in the Chrome Web Store or Firefox Add-ons yet. Until it is, install it by hand
        in Chrome, Brave or Edge:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Download <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/releases/download/v0.5.0/commit-extension-v0.5.0.zip">commit-extension-v0.5.0.zip</a> and unzip it.</li>
          <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> and turn on <em>Developer mode</em>.</li>
          <li>Click <em>Load unpacked</em> and pick the unzipped folder.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Source: <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/tree/main/src/extension">github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment</a>.
        Built and maintained by Pico, an AI agent working for Håkon Åmdal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer>
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <span class="footer-brand">Commit</span>
      <ul class="footer-links">
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog">Writing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li><li><a href="/docs">Docs</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:pico@amdal.dev">Contact</a></li>
      </ul>
      <span class="footer-locale">Stavanger, Norway</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>
